---
import Layout from "../../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import digitalMarketingFront from "../../../assets/images/services/digital-marketing-front.png";
import digitalMarketingMiddle from "../../../assets/images/services/digital-marketing-middle.png";
import digitalMarketingBack from "../../../assets/images/services/digital-marketing-back.jpg";
import digitalMarketingOffice from "../../../assets/images/services/digital-marketing-office-photo.jpg";
import "../../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Digital Marketing Strategy &amp; Campaigns | Kelp Agency"
  description="Kelp connects audience research, paid campaigns, content, landing pages, and reporting so your marketing drives qualified enquiries and sales."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Services"
    title="Digital Marketing"
    description="Digital marketing works when the strategy is specific, the message is clear, and the next move is measurable. We build marketing systems around the real problem your business needs to solve."
    mediaFront={digitalMarketingFront}
    mediaFrontWidth={1300}
    mediaFrontHeight={1300}
    mediaMiddle={digitalMarketingMiddle}
    mediaMiddleWidth={1300}
    mediaMiddleHeight={1300}
    mediaBack={digitalMarketingBack}
    mediaBackWidth={1300}
    mediaBackHeight={1300}
  />
  <div class="service-intro service-intro--marketing">
    <div class="wrapper">
      <p class="h4">
        Most marketing problems are really diagnosis problems. If the audience
        is off, the message is vague, or the reporting does not lead to action,
        more activity will not fix it.
      </p>
      <div class="service-intro-media" data-lg-parallax="child">
        <div>
          <Picture
            src={digitalMarketingOffice}
            alt="Kelpers reviewing marketing analytics"
            loading="lazy"
            width={866}
            height={866}
            widths={[480, 720, 866]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
            inferSize
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-intro-text">
        <p>
          We start by identifying what is actually broken, then shape the
          strategy, execution, and reporting around a clearer goal. That is how
          campaigns become easier to improve over time instead of harder to
          explain.
        </p>
        <p>
          We can support your in-house team, take ownership of specific
          channels, or manage the full campaign rhythm for you depending on
          where the bottleneck really is.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="service-list services-list--marketing wrapper">
    <h2>Digital Marketing</h2>
    <div class="service-list-item">
      <div data-lg-parallax data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.2">
        <div
          class="service-list-item-square"
          style="background-color: var(--light-green)"
          data-lg-reveal="layer-to-right"
        ></div>
      </div>
      <div
        data-lg-parallax
        data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.4"
        data-lg-lottie="/animations/audience-targeting.json"
        data-lg-lottie-autoplay="true"
        data-lg-lottie-loop="true"
        data-lg-lottie-lazy="true"
        class="service-list-item-icon"
      ></div>
      <h3 class="h4">
        <a href="/services/audience-targeting/">Audience Targeting</a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        Marketing gets expensive fast when you are talking to everyone. Audience
        targeting helps narrow the message to the people most likely to care and
        convert.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="service-list-item">
      <div data-lg-parallax data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.2">
        <div
          class="service-list-item-square"
          style="background-color: var(--light-green)"
          data-lg-reveal="layer-to-right"
        ></div>
      </div>
      <div
        data-lg-parallax
        data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.4"
        data-lg-lottie="/animations/campaign-management.json"
        data-lg-lottie-autoplay="true"
        data-lg-lottie-loop="true"
        data-lg-lottie-lazy="true"
        class="service-list-item-icon"
      ></div>
      <h3 class="h4">
        <a href="/services/campaign-management/">Campaign Management</a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        Campaigns work better when the timeline, message, assets, and budget
        move in the same direction instead of fighting each other.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="service-list-item">
      <div data-lg-parallax data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.2">
        <div
          class="service-list-item-square"
          style="background-color: var(--light-green)"
          data-lg-reveal="layer-to-right"
        ></div>
      </div>
      <div
        data-lg-parallax
        data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.4"
        data-lg-lottie="/animations/social-ppc.json"
        data-lg-lottie-autoplay="true"
        data-lg-lottie-loop="true"
        data-lg-lottie-lazy="true"
        class="service-list-item-icon"
      ></div>
      <h3 class="h4">
        <a href="/services/social-ppc/">Social & PPC</a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        Paid media only works when the targeting, creative, and landing
        experience support the same goal.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="service-list-item">
      <div data-lg-parallax data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.2">
        <div
          class="service-list-item-square"
          style="background-color: var(--light-green)"
          data-lg-reveal="layer-to-right"
        ></div>
      </div>
      <div
        data-lg-parallax
        data-lg-parallax-amplitude="0.4"
        data-lg-lottie="/animations/reporting.json"
        data-lg-lottie-autoplay="true"
        data-lg-lottie-loop="true"
        data-lg-lottie-lazy="true"
        class="service-list-item-icon"
      ></div>
      <h3 class="h4">
        <a href="/services/reporting/">Reporting</a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        Reporting should make the next decision clearer, not just give you more
        charts to stare at.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Marketing can be active without being coordinated. A paid campaign
        targets one audience, the website speaks to another, content answers
        questions nobody is asking, and reports stop at clicks. Leaders then
        face a choice of spending more or stopping work without knowing what is
        actually limiting results.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
      <p>
        We start with a business outcome and trace the path back through the
        website, message, channel, and audience. Then we set priorities for
        campaigns, content, landing pages, and measurement. Kelp can lead the
        full program or work with an internal team, with regular reviews of lead
        quality and customer behavior.
      </p>
      <h2>Find the Actual Constraint</h2>
      <p>
        We look at where qualified prospects are lost. The problem may be
        targeting, an unclear offer, weak creative, a landing page that does not
        match the ad, or tracking that cannot distinguish a good lead from a
        form submission. Fixing that constraint is usually more valuable than
        adding another channel.
      </p>
      <h2>Build a Plan the Team Can Improve</h2>
      <p>
        Our work can include audience targeting, campaign management, paid
        search and social, copy, creative, and reporting. We review qualified
        enquiries or sales alongside spend and traffic, then use what we learn
        to refine the campaign and site together. <a href="/work/elev8-fun/">Elev8 Fun</a> shows how Kelp
        brought digital design, campaigns, paid social, website work, and
        support into one engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        If marketing performance has become difficult to explain, talk through
        the customer journey with Kelp.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Measure Progress</h2>
      <p>
        We agree on a useful business outcome before choosing campaign metrics.
        Depending on the work, that may mean qualified enquiries, booked
        conversations, purchases, or repeat orders. We look at those outcomes
        alongside cost, traffic quality, and the steps between first visit and
        conversion. The result is a practical review of what improved and what
        still needs attention.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Audience and offer research</li>
        <li>Paid search, paid social, and campaign planning</li>
        <li>Landing-page, copy, and creative coordination</li>
        <li>Reporting tied to qualified enquiries or sales</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the channels you use, the leads or sales you want more of, and the
        reports you currently trust. We can identify a focused first improvement
        before building a wider marketing plan.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Do we need to use every channel?</h3>
      <p>
        No. We recommend channels that fit how your customers discover and
        evaluate the offer, then expand only when the current path is working
        and measurable.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style lang="scss">
  .service-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4rem;
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin-bottom: 8rem;
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      margin-bottom: 4rem;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    h2 {
      flex: 1 1 100%;
      text-align: center;
      max-width: none;
      margin-top: 8rem;
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
      @media (max-width: 767px) {
        margin-top: 5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
      }
    }
    &-item {
      flex: 1 1 400px;
      position: relative;
      p {
        max-width: 50ch;
      }
      &-square {
        width: 103px;
        height: 103px;
        left: 0;
        z-index: -1;
        top: 0;
        background: var(--light-teal);
      }
      &-icon {
        display: block;
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        max-width: 120px;
        max-height: 120px;
      }
    }
  }
  .service-intro {
    background: var(--lighter-teal);
    padding: 8rem 0;
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      padding-bottom: 4rem;
    }
    .wrapper {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 2rem 3rem;
    }
    .h4 {
      flex: 1 1 100%;
      color: var(--purple);
      max-width: 52ch;
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 5rem;
    }
    &-media {
      flex: 1 1 400px;
    }
    &-text {
      flex: 1 1 400px;
      p {
        max-width: none;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
